Back-port the client side of gophertunnel's modern offline login to v1.57.1.

PocketMine-MP 5.44.3 speaks protocol 1001, the protocol of gophertunnel v1.57.1, but rejects that release's offline
login. It expects the client data fields and identity token claims that gophertunnel adopted in v1.58.0. This patch
applies these upstream changes to v1.57.1:

  * 654cd5f "protocol/login: Fix modern self-signed login claims" (#468), in full. The self-signed identity token
    gets the multiplayer audience and carries the player UUID as "leguuid", and the client data sends
    FilterProfanity, ClientEditorConnectionIntent and ClientIsEditorCapable instead of IsEditorMode.
  * b36ddad "minecraft: Update protocol to 1.26.40" (#481), only the ClientData.ProfileHash field.

Left out on purpose: the login parsing changes made to the same files between v1.57.1 and v1.58.0 (#474 and the
Validate part of #481), because the bot never parses a login, and ClientData.Nonce from #501, because it is
omitempty and the bot never sets it, so it never reaches the wire.

Upstream:  https://github.com/Sandertv/gophertunnel/pull/468 and https://github.com/Sandertv/gophertunnel/pull/481
Test:      TestLoginRequestFormat in bots/legacy1001 fails against unpatched v1.57.1.
Drop when: the pinned PocketMine-MP accepts the protocol bots/loadbot speaks. bots/legacy1001 goes with it.

diff --git a/minecraft/protocol/login/data.go b/minecraft/protocol/login/data.go
index 198e39f..c0e30b7 100644
--- a/minecraft/protocol/login/data.go
+++ b/minecraft/protocol/login/data.go
@@ -140,8 +140,12 @@ type ClientData struct {
 	// GUIScale is the GUI scale of the player. It is by default 0, and is otherwise -1 or -2 for a smaller
 	// GUI scale than usual.
 	GUIScale int `json:"GuiScale"`
-	// IsEditorMode is a value to dictate if the player is in editor mode.
-	IsEditorMode bool
+	// FilterProfanity indicates if the client has profanity filtering enabled.
+	FilterProfanity bool
+	// ClientEditorConnectionIntent indicates how the client intends to connect to an editor world.
+	ClientEditorConnectionIntent int
+	// ClientIsEditorCapable specifies if the client supports editor features.
+	ClientIsEditorCapable bool
 	// LanguageCode is the language code of the player. It looks like 'en_UK'. It follows the ISO language
 	// codes, but hyphens ('-') are replaced with underscores. ('_')
 	LanguageCode string
@@ -246,6 +250,8 @@ type ClientData struct {
 	PartyID string `json:"PartyId"`
 	// PartyLeader is if the client is the leader of the party they are in.
 	PartyLeader bool `json:"IsPartyLeader"`
+	// ProfileHash is a client-generated hash of the equipped persona skin.
+	ProfileHash string `json:"ProfileHash"`
 }
 
 // PersonaPiece represents a piece of a persona skin. All pieces are sent separately.
diff --git a/minecraft/protocol/login/request.go b/minecraft/protocol/login/request.go
index fa8c8cb..d6c4039 100644
--- a/minecraft/protocol/login/request.go
+++ b/minecraft/protocol/login/request.go
@@ -405,6 +405,7 @@ func EncodeOffline(identityData IdentityData, data ClientData, key *ecdsa.Privat
 		req.Certificate = certificate{Chain: chain{chainJWT}}
 		req.Legacy = true
 	} else {
+		claims.Audience = jwt.Audience{"api://auth-minecraft-services/multiplayer"}
 		req.Certificate = certificate{Chain: chain{""}}
 		req.Token, _ = jwt.Signed(signer).Claims(tokenClaims{
 			Claims:          claims,
@@ -447,7 +448,7 @@ type tokenClaims struct {
 	DisplayName string `json:"xname"`
 	// Identity is the UUID of the player. It is only set for offline logins where
 	// the UUID cannot be derived from the XUID.
-	Identity string `json:"identity,omitempty"`
+	Identity string `json:"leguuid,omitempty"`
 }
 
 // identityData converts the OIDC tokenClaims into IdentityData.
